## Fraktur / Historical German Books (Google Books)

Fraktur-printed German books from Google Books produce consistent OCR artefacts (merged words, dropped spaces, library-stamp debris). See `references/fraktur-ocr-cleaning.md` for a systematic cleanup workflow covering:

- Regex-based missing-space repair (lowercase↔uppercase, period boundaries)
- Hyphenated compound re-joining (distinct from intended hyphens)
- Type-3 lowercase-lowercase merges (dictionary and frequency approaches)
- Google Books front-matter stripping (license pages, library stamps, title-page debris)
- Structural mapping of George-Kreis style headings (`ERSTES BUCH` → `#` headings)

The reference file includes detection patterns and a quality-check workflow. Bookmark it before starting any pre-1945 German PDF extraction.

## Notes

- `web_extract` is always first choice for URLs
- pymupdf is the safe default — instant, no models, works everywhere
- marker-pdf is for OCR, scanned docs, equations, complex layouts — install only when needed
- Both helper scripts accept `--help` for full usage
- marker-pdf downloads ~2.5GB of models to `~/.cache/huggingface/` on first use
- For Word docs: `pip install python-docx` (better than OCR — parses actual structure)
- For PowerPoint: see the `powerpoint` skill (uses python-pptx)
- **Fraktur tip**: Google Books pre-1924 German PDFs are text-based (not scanned), so pymupdf alone suffices — marker-pdf would add ~3GB models for no benefit.
- **Book OCR template**: `templates/ocr-volume.sh` has the canonical page-at-a-time, resume-aware, trap EXIT scaffolding. Copy + edit paths for any new OCR project.
- **Multi-volume projects**: Create kanban cards per volume for visibility. Never run in parallel on constrained systems.
- **⚠️ Resume-by-last-page gap failure**: The canonical resume pattern (`LAST=$(grep ... | tail -1)`) fails when the output has gaps — pages that were never processed but a later page marker exists. The script exits saying "already complete" while pages are missing. Always check for gaps before trusting resume: `grep "^=== PAGE" "$OUT" | sed 's/=== PAGE //;s/ ===//' | sort -n | awk 'NR>1{for(i=prev+1;i<$1;i++) print "GAP:", i} {prev=$1}'`. See `references/batch-ocr-pipeline.md` → "Resume-by-last-page failure with gaps" for detection, the sed truncation fix, and the `at now` persistence pattern for long runs.
- **Disk check**: Always `df -h /` before starting batch OCR. This VPS has 38GB root — one volume at ~9GB temp can fill it if other services are running.